208. In any Court to which he is appointed, the Registrar
in Chambers may—

(a) adjourn any proceedings;
(b) fix a date for the trial of any proceedings;
(c) administer oaths for affidavits and take bonds;

(d) where security is ordered, determine its
sufficiency and require sureties to justify;

(e) by consent of all parties, order consolidation
of any proceedings; and

(f) carry out any other functions provided under
this Act or any order of a Judge.
